---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Thermodynamics Laws Cheat Sheet | Free Zeroth, First, Second, Third"
  description="Complete thermodynamics laws cheat sheet with zeroth, first, second, and third laws. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Thermodynamics Laws<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Zeroth, first, second, and third laws. From thermal equilibrium to entropy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Zeroth Law</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Thermal Equilibrium</h3>
        <pre><code>If A = B and B = C, then A = C
Thermal equilibrium is transitive
Basis for temperature measurement
Temperature is the property that is equal in equilibrium</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>First Law</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Energy Conservation</h3>
        <pre><code>ΔU = Q - W
Internal energy = heat added - work done
Energy is conserved
ΔU depends only on initial and final states</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Second Law</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Entropy Increase</h3>
        <pre><code>ΔS ≥ 0 (isolated system)
Entropy always increases or stays constant
No perfect heat engine (100% efficiency)
No perfect refrigerator (no work input)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Clausius Statement</h3>
        <pre><code>Heat cannot spontaneously flow from cold to hot
Requires external work
Refrigerator&#58; Q_c/W ≤ T_c/(T_h - T_c)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third Law</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Absolute Zero</h3>
        <pre><code>S → 0 as T → 0
Entropy approaches zero at absolute zero
Absolute zero is unattainable
Only approachable asymptotically</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Applications</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Heat Engines</h3>
        <pre><code>η = W/Q_h = 1 - Q_c/Q_h
η_Carnot = 1 - T_c/T_h (maximum efficiency)
T must be in Kelvin
Real engines&#58; η < η_Carnot</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
